# broiler-js unicode data pin 1
#
# The Unicode Character Database files the JavaScript profile's Unicode tables are generated
# from, and the Unicode licence text from the same site. Decision JSD-0031 section 5 asks for
# them to be retrieved once, hashed, archived beside this file and read by nothing but the
# generator, which lives in the architecture test project and refuses any file whose bytes or
# header do not match what is recorded here. Rule N22 holds the archive, the generated tables and
# this file to each other.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Retrieved twice on 2026-09-22 by Claude, with the repository owner's explicit
# permission given in conversation on that day, into two separate directories; `diff -r` over the
# two found them byte-identical, and every figure below is a reading of the first copy, which is
# the copy archived here. The three ECMAScript property tables JSD-0031 adds to the retrieval list
# were retrieved in the same two passes from tc39/ecma262 at the archived edition's revision and
# are archived beside that edition in src/Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript/docs/specification/, not
# here; they are pinned below by repository-relative path because the generator reads them too.
#
# SpecialCasing.txt WAS ADDED ON 2026-10-03, from the same source, version and site, retrieved twice
# by Claude into two directories and found byte-identical, and archived unmodified. The repository
# owner asked that day for the JavaScript profile's roadmap to be continued, and the recommendation
# written into JSD-0031 the same day names this file as the next input; no permission specific to
# this retrieval was given, and that is recorded here rather than implied. It feeds the full case
# mappings of toUpperCase and toLowerCase and the non-u Canonicalize (JSD-0027 slice N2).
#
# emoji-sequences.txt AND emoji-zwj-sequences.txt WERE ADDED ON 2026-10-04, from the same release's
# `emoji/` directory rather than its `ucd/` one, which is why they sit under emoji-17.0.0/ and the
# `emoji-source` line names where they came from. Each was retrieved twice by Claude into two
# directories, found byte-identical, and archived unmodified. They define the seven properties of
# strings the `v` flag admits (phase F2 of the roadmap's section 26, which names exactly these two
# files). The repository owner asked that day for the roadmap's phases to be continued; no permission
# specific to this retrieval was given, and that is recorded here rather than implied.
#
# THE SIX auxiliary/ FILES OF UAX #29 WERE ADDED ON 2026-10-04: GraphemeBreakProperty.txt,
# WordBreakProperty.txt and SentenceBreakProperty.txt, from which Intl.Segmenter's break tables are
# generated into the Intl data assembly (decision JSD-0050), and GraphemeBreakTest.txt,
# WordBreakTest.txt and SentenceBreakTest.txt, which are test-only conformance input like
# NormalizationTest.txt. Each was retrieved twice by Claude from the same source, version and site
# into two directories, found byte-identical, and archived unmodified. The repository owner asked for
# the roadmap's phases to be continued; no permission specific to this retrieval was given, and that
# is recorded here rather than implied.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. `file <path relative to this directory> <bytes> <sha256>` for a UCD file or
# the licence text; `spec-table <path relative to the repository root> <bytes> <sha256>` for an
# ECMAScript property table. UnicodeData.txt carries no header line and is held by its hash alone;
# every other UCD file's first line names its version and the generator refuses one that does not
# name the pinned version. NormalizationTest.txt is test-only input: no table is generated from it.

data unicode-character-database
version 17.0.0
source https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/
licence-source https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
emoji-source https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/emoji/
spec-table-source https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tc39/ecma262/0248456c758431e4bb8e5d26333ff1865123c9cd/
retrieved 2026-09-22
retrievals 2 byte-identical
archived yes
